---
// Real sky behind the whole website (owner request, Oct 2026): a time-lapse of real cumulus clouds (Pexels, credited
// on /credits via src/data/vision-media.json → vision.sky-clouds) on one fixed layer under every page. Light sections
// are a translucent wash over it (global.css), so soft clouds drift behind them while scrolling, and the first section
// of a page opens onto the full sky; dark sections stay solid. It sits outside the Barba container, so it keeps
// playing across page transitions (src/scripts/chrome/sky.js). Reduced motion: the still first frame only.
---
<div class="sky" data-sky aria-hidden="true">
  <picture>
    <source media="(orientation: portrait)" srcset="/media/sky/sky-poster-m.webp" />
    <img class="sky__still" src="/media/sky/sky-poster.webp" alt="" decoding="async" />
  </picture>
  <video class="sky__film" muted playsinline loop preload="none" data-src="/media/sky/sky.mp4" data-src-mobile="/media/sky/sky-m.mp4"></video>
</div>

<style is:global>
  .sky { position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: -1; overflow: hidden; pointer-events: none; background: #8fb4df; }
  .sky__still, .sky__film { position: absolute; inset: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; object-fit: cover; object-position: 50% 30%; }
  .sky__film { opacity: 0; transition: opacity 1.2s ease; }
  .sky__film.is-playing { opacity: 1; }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .sky__film { display: none; } }
</style>
